> >NIST's international standing, which was already lying down, to
> >paraphrase a great American poet.
>
> Do you have any concrete examples? I think it is nearly impossible to add=
ress all comments, as many of them are mutually contradictory. Based on my =
personal experience, I believe NIST pays close attention to the feedback it=
 receives and makes reasonable trade-offs. Overall, I think most people are=
 quite satisfied with NIST=E2=80=99s PQC project. At least, NIST offers pub=
lic email lists, workshops, comment periods, and specifications, something =
that organizations such as ISO and ECCG do not.
